  "summary": "An AFSC guest columnist urges Denver City Council to reject Mayor Mike Johnston's proposed Axon ALPR contract, arguing that although the council previously ended Denver's Flock contracts, Axon poses similar surveillance, ICE-cooperation, and civil-liberties risks given its federal DHS/ICE contracts and leadership ties.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Over the last year, organizations like mine, the American Friends Service Committee (AFSC), successfully organized to end Denver's contracts with one such company, Flock.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Axon currently has a $370 million contract to provide ICE and DHS with body cameras, TASERs, and other devices and technologies.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "For the safety of our community and the protection of our civil liberties, the City Council must vote against a contract with Axon.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
